  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A very long straight conducting wire, lying along the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math>-axis, carries a current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>. The integral <math> <mrow> <mo>∫</mo> <mover accent=\"true\"> <mo>B</mo> <mo>→</mo> </mover> <mo>.</mo> <mo>d</mo> <mover accent=\"true\"> <mi>ℓ</mi> <mo>→</mo> </mover> </mrow> </math> is computed along the straight line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PQ</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>&nbsp;has the coordinates <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math>&nbsp;has the coordinates <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. The integral has the magnitude (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>)</p>\r",
